# AI-Based Smart Road Defect Detection & Predictive Maintenance Platform
## Initial Setup & System Architecture Documentation (`initialsetup.docs`)
**Date:** September 30, 2026  
**System Status:** Stage 1 Foundation & End-to-End Pipeline Operational  
**Test Suite Coverage:** 35 / 35 Passing Tests (100%)

---

## 1. Executive Summary

The **AI-Based Smart Road Defect Detection & Predictive Maintenance Platform** is an intelligent civil engineering infrastructure solution. It bridges the gap between high-frequency computer vision surface inspection and long-term economic pavement maintenance scheduling.

Using road inspection dashcam video feeds, the platform:
1. **Detects & Tracks Defects:** Quantifies unsealed utility digs, deteriorated asphalt patches, structural cracks, and cavities/potholes using Ultralytics YOLOv8 and OpenCV spatial tracking.
2. **Computes Pavement Condition Index (PCI):** Calculates a standardized structural health score ($0.0 - 100.0$) using weighted deduct values.
3. **Classifies Urgency Tiers:** Categorizes road sections into standardized maintenance priority bands.
4. **Optimizes Interventions via Reinforcement Learning:** Feeds a 5-element state vector into a Deep Q-Network (DQN) policy trained in a custom Gymnasium environment to recommend the most cost-effective action (*Do Nothing*, *Preventive Repair*, or *Major Resurfacing*).
5. **Serves Multi-Interface Consumers:** Exposes high-throughput REST endpoints via FastAPI and an interactive real-time control center via Streamlit.

